1
00:00:00,139 --> 00:00:04,330
When a customer clicks a Klick-Zen button
in your email, what do they see next?

2
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:09,139
A landing page. In the next few minutes,
we'll make it look and sound like your

3
00:00:09,139 --> 00:00:11,115
brand, with no web design needed.

4
00:00:11,195 --> 00:00:15,558
Clicking any link in an email opens a web
browser, and Klick-Zen buttons are no

5
00:00:15,558 --> 00:00:19,258
different. That visit is what tells
Klick-Zen to update the ticket.

6
00:00:19,338 --> 00:00:23,845
The landing page is what your customer
sees next: clear confirmation that their

7
00:00:23,845 --> 00:00:26,640
click worked, instead of a blank tab or an
error.

8
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:31,306
Klick-Zen hosts it for you, and it reads
clearly on phones and desktops alike.

9
00:00:31,306 --> 00:00:33,776
There's nothing to build or host yourself.

10
00:00:33,856 --> 00:00:38,560
To make it yours, open Klick-Zen in
Zendesk, and click Default Landing Page in

11
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:39,706
the left-hand menu.

12
00:00:39,786 --> 00:00:44,731
There are two pages here, a Confirmation
page and a Ticket Closed page, and one set

13
00:00:44,731 --> 00:00:47,174
of global settings that styles them both.

14
00:00:47,254 --> 00:00:51,710
Start with the Global Landing Page
Settings. The HTML Browser Title is the

15
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:54,781
text in the browser tab, usually your
company name.

16
00:00:54,861 --> 00:01:00,058
Next, the Template Colors. The Brand Color
draws the bold outlines, so it's usually

17
00:01:00,058 --> 00:01:01,686
the darker of your colors.

18
00:01:01,766 --> 00:01:06,857
The Accent Color sits behind the text, and
the Text Color is the text itself. Choose

19
00:01:06,857 --> 00:01:08,493
a pair that's easy to read.

20
00:01:08,573 --> 00:01:15,113
Then the Page Header Image, usually your
logo. Click Select new image, and choose a

21
00:01:15,113 --> 00:01:17,792
JPG, GIF or PNG up to 3 megabytes.

22
00:01:17,872 --> 00:01:21,821
Now the Confirmation page. It's shown
while the ticket is still active, to let

23
00:01:21,821 --> 00:01:24,201
your customer know their response went
through.

24
00:01:24,281 --> 00:01:28,754
Type your message on the left using simple
markdown, and the preview on the right

25
00:01:28,754 --> 00:01:30,024
shows how it will look.

26
00:01:30,104 --> 00:01:34,909
The toolbar adds common formatting for
you, such as bold text or a bulleted list.

27
00:01:34,989 --> 00:01:40,761
For security, active content like HTML,
JavaScript and CSS is never rendered, so

28
00:01:40,761 --> 00:01:43,575
the page stays safe for every customer.

29
00:01:43,655 --> 00:01:47,816
The Ticket Closed page appears when the
ticket is no longer active, for example

30
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:49,976
when it's already been solved and closed.

31
00:01:50,056 --> 00:01:54,624
It lets your customer know their click
can't change anything now, so a helpful

32
00:01:54,624 --> 00:01:56,440
next step here goes a long way.

33
00:01:56,520 --> 00:02:01,273
The Preview this page button stays greyed
out until your changes are saved. So click

34
00:02:01,273 --> 00:02:03,197
Update, at the bottom of the page.

35
00:02:03,277 --> 00:02:08,421
Now click Preview this page, and see the
finished page exactly as your customers

36
00:02:08,421 --> 00:02:08,743
will.

37
00:02:08,823 --> 00:02:11,316
So when your customer clicks a button in
your email,

38
00:02:11,396 --> 00:02:16,219
they land on a page with your logo, your
colors and your words, in a browser tab

39
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:17,726
with your company's name.

40
00:02:17,806 --> 00:02:21,996
And if they click a button on a ticket
that's already closed, your Ticket Closed

41
00:02:21,996 --> 00:02:23,672
page tells them what to do next.

42
00:02:23,752 --> 00:02:28,950
That's landing pages: a clear, friendly
answer to every click, in your own brand,

43
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:30,297
with nothing to host.

44
00:02:30,377 --> 00:02:34,663
Want to go further? Use your own
subdomain, or send customers to a page of

45
00:02:34,663 --> 00:02:39,007
your own, such as a help article or a
survey, for every button or just one.

46
00:02:39,087 --> 00:02:44,052
Find Klick-Zen on the Zendesk Marketplace,
and make every click feel like part of

47
00:02:44,052 --> 00:02:44,726
your brand.
